{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Economy log: mail sent and taken, and mail from the server, are logged",
  "contract": [
    "With the economy log on, a player mail writes mail_send rows for the sender, one per item and one for the money; the receiver writes mail_take rows when they take the money and the items. A mail the sender cannot pay for writes nothing.",
    "A mail that no player sent (the Postmaster returning an item) writes a system_mail row for its receiver when it is sent and a mail_take row when the item is taken; a player's mail is never a system_mail.",
    "The sender mails a Peacebloom (2447) and 100 copper to a character on its own account (no delivery delay); the Postmaster mails that character a Silverleaf (765). Both characters start at level 20, so each also gets the level mail with a Riding Training Pamphlet (46875, Randal Hunter 4732), another system_mail row.",
    "Returning a mail is not a send: the returned mail reaches the original sender as a system_mail, and the character who returned it writes no mail_send row. Each player-mail row names the other character and account; a taken item keeps its GUID.",
    "A mail the server sends with the receiver as its own sender (as the Welcome Warchest and the Call Board cache do) is a system_mail, and taking it names no other character.",
    "Cash on delivery: the sender mails a Briarthorn (2450) for 50 copper; the receiver's take names the sender, the payment the server mails back is the receiver's mail_send of 50 copper to the sender, and the sender's take of that payment names the receiver."
  ],
  "timeout_ms": 90000,
  "economy_log": true,
  "players": [
    {
      "id": "sender",
      "name": "Coaelmails",
      "race": 1,
      "class": 1,
      "level": 20
    },
    {
      "id": "alt",
      "name": "Coaelmailr",
      "race": 1,
      "class": 1,
      "level": 20,
      "account_of": "sender"
    }
